From: Kian Linux build <buildroot@kianriscv.local>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/unix: gate Bluetooth source files on MICROPY_PY_BLUETOOTH

The unix port's Makefile unconditionally lists the BTstack / NimBLE
glue source files (mpbthciport.c, mpbtstackport_*.c, mpnimbleport.c)
in SRC_C, which makes them visible to the QSTR preprocess pass even
when MICROPY_PY_BLUETOOTH=0. On a no-pthread / no-libusb cross
target (here: riscv32 uClibc no-MMU FLAT) the preprocessor then
fails on missing <pthread.h> / <libusb-1.0/libusb.h> includes:

    mpbtstackport_h4.c:27: fatal error: pthread.h: No such file
    mpbtstackport_usb.c:27: fatal error: pthread.h: No such file

Wrap the five BT-glue source files in an
ifeq ($(MICROPY_PY_BLUETOOTH),1) block so they are only added to the
build when Bluetooth is actually enabled. This matches how every
other optional module (FFI, JNI, termios, socket, ...) is handled
just above in the same Makefile.

Upstream MicroPython has reorganized the unix Makefile substantially
since 1.19.1; this patch is a minimal back-port of the same gating
idea for 1.19.1 so we can build with MICROPY_PY_BLUETOOTH=0.

Signed-off-by: Kian Linux build <buildroot@kianriscv.local>
---
 ports/unix/Makefile | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ports/unix/Makefile b/ports/unix/Makefile
--- a/ports/unix/Makefile
+++ b/ports/unix/Makefile
@@ -229,13 +229,17 @@ SRC_C += \
 	moduselect.c \
 	alloc.c \
 	fatfs_port.c \
+	$(SRC_MOD) \
+	$(wildcard $(VARIANT_DIR)/*.c)
+
+ifeq ($(MICROPY_PY_BLUETOOTH),1)
+SRC_C += \
 	mpbthciport.c \
 	mpbtstackport_common.c \
 	mpbtstackport_h4.c \
 	mpbtstackport_usb.c \
-	mpnimbleport.c \
-	$(SRC_MOD) \
-	$(wildcard $(VARIANT_DIR)/*.c)
+	mpnimbleport.c
+endif

 SHARED_SRC_C += $(addprefix shared/,\
 	runtime/gchelper_generic.c \
--
2.40.0
